{
  "errors": [
    {
      "span": "On account of (the statement of) the trembling (of the world) i.e., impelling of the world to action (Vajra is Brahman only).",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "span": "From the predicate, 'trembles,' the energetic Vajra can only be the perfect Lord.",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "span": "\" Who indeed could make the world live and live well, if this Akasa (the Lord shining everywhere) were not bliss itself\" (Tait. II. 7)",
      "category": "addition",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "span": "\" He is the breath of the breath, he is the eye of the eye.\"",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "span": "Bri. VI. iv. 18).",
      "category": "omission",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "span": "\"Even the movements of the Air are well under the control of the glorious Lord Hari. Then what can be said of the movements of the rest of the world whose activity is guided by the Air.\"",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "span": "“The Lord is called (Chakra) a ‘discus’ because he propels (the soul into the embodied life); and He is called Vajra because he is avoided by the Daityas or unapproached by defects. He is called the ‘sword’ because he slays (destroys) the sinful; thus the Lord alone is declared by the names of all the weapons.”",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "span": "The Brahma Vaivarta Purana.",
      "category": "omission",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "span": "It has been said that the Light which is placed in the heart is Paramatman (the highest Lord); with regard to this Light, in continuation of the text,",
      "category": "addition",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "span": "\" He who is perfect in knowledge, who dwells in the organs of sense and the heart; who is the perfect Self,\"",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "span": "\" He goes in turn through the two worlds\" (Bri. VI. iii. 7)",
      "category": "accuracy",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "span": "from this statement, the individual soul seems to be meant. To remove this doubt the Sutrakara says:",
      "category": "omission",
      "severity": "major"
    }
  ]
}
